{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite","id":1451194,"title":"First 16th Generation Cainite","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-07T03:43:59-07:00","id":1451194,"title":"First 16th Generation Cainite","content":"To clarify I am using all of oWoD splats (and often run crossover games). I was wondering who was the first 16th Generation Cainite (and when/where it happened). I got an idea about a student who was part of Anagath F45.6 testing (Magadon Inc. product, based on Giovanni blood). The first generation of F45.6 was too strong thus changed him into a Thin-Blood. Another idea is to use Blacklight 24 laboratory (from V5 loresheet) where the governement tried to create some kind of human superweapon. The problem is that I still use older editions of Vampire (because there's no 5th Edition Werewolf, Mage or Wraith) and have a little problem with conversion this idea into sheet and pencil (especially Blood Potency). How would you deal with this problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T07:11:20-07:00","id":1451208,"title":"","content":"I would think the first 16th Gen. Cainite would be a woman successfully Embraced in L.A. by a 15th Gen. Thin-Blooded Anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T10:38:47-07:00","id":1451235,"title":"","content":"I think it might be mentioned in Beckett's Jyhad Diary?<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for Blood Potency, if you search on here you'll find some nifty conversions for bringing it into V20 mechanics. That gives you a few choices.<br /> <br /> If you want a ready-made solution, use this one: <a href=\"https://static1.squarespace.com/static/513f57ebe4b0970eaf232dec/t/5c05ae8f898583fc3fb57776/1543876240815/V5%2Bto%2BV20%2BConversion%2BDoc.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://static1.squarespace.com/stat...sion%2BDoc.pdf</a><br /> <br /> ETA: There are also feeding Flaws that relate to losing the ability to eat from animals or humans, or vitae Flaws that give you weaker blood if you'd rather focus on simulating those effects without bringing in BP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-07-2021, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T12:08:26-07:00","id":1451240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451235#post1451235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it might be mentioned in Beckett's Jyhad Diary?<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for Blood Potency, if you search on here you'll find some nifty conversions for bringing it into V20 mechanics. That gives you a few choices.<br /> <br /> If you want a ready-made solution, use this one: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/513f57ebe4b0970eaf232dec/t/5c05ae8f898583fc3fb57776/1543876240815/V5%2Bto%2BV20%2BConversion%2BDoc.pdf&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://static1.squarespace.com/stat...sion%2BDoc.pdf</a><br /> <br /> ETA: There are also feeding Flaws that relate to losing the ability to eat from animals or humans, or vitae Flaws that give you weaker blood if you'd rather focus on simulating those effects without bringing in BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right! I thought I remembered reading it somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T13:13:46-07:00","id":1451248,"title":"","content":"Thx for your answers. To be honest I wasn't asking who was the first 16th Generation canonically but rather how to create the first one using one of those ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T15:29:50-07:00","id":1451260,"title":"","content":"Mechanics wise idk enough about V5 to help you. Lorewise I\u2019m not sure if either of those ideas would help you. Generation is passed down from Kindred to Kindred to indicate their distance from Caine, and an artificially created serum wouldn\u2019t necessarily (or even likely) create a vampire with such a high Generation. But good luck. Keep us posted on how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T15:35:28-07:00","id":1451261,"title":"","content":"Do you have mechanics for 15 gen same limitations except you can only have up to level 2 disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though honestly if you had a successful Artifical Embrace via technology i'd just make a much more legtimate gen since that's how its worked for every other paradigm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T15:43:26-07:00","id":1451262,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t. Not offhand. But I agree with your second paragraph.<br /> <br /> Have a great night. Ttyl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T16:36:43-07:00","id":1451267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451260#post1451260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanics wise idk enough about V5 to help you. Lorewise I\u2019m not sure if either of those ideas would help you. Generation is passed down from Kindred to Kindred to indicate their distance from Caine, and an artificially created serum wouldn\u2019t necessarily (or even likely) create a vampire with such a high Generation. But good luck. Keep us posted on how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there was an adventure (by Atlas Games if I remember correctly) where a PCs were artificially embraced becoming 13 Generation Cainites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T16:52:01-07:00","id":1451268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451267#post1451267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there was an adventure (by Atlas Games if I remember correctly) where a PCs were artificially embraced becoming 13 Generation Cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At least One clan and one major bloodline were created via another paradigm of Magic. While there does seem to be a certain amount of not creating power from nothing it wasn't automaticaly the bottom.<br /> <br /> Considering Nectar was an outgrowth of this technique I'd argue if you have a 13th gen vampire to start.. you get 13th gen vampires.. if you have something lower well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T19:43:13-07:00","id":1451278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451261#post1451261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have mechanics for 15 gen same limitations except you can only have up to level 2 disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though honestly if you had a successful Artifical Embrace via technology i'd just make a much more legtimate gen since that's how its worked for every other paradigm</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinbloods don't have disciplines in V5 they have their own special powers. <br /> <br /> OP:<br /> From Vampire: Just hand wave it as that's how it worked, nothing in vampire really covers this except for specifically disallowing it in some editions (has to be drank from the vein of the vampire).<br /> <br /> From a Mage: Prime 5, Matter 4 and Life 4 effect minimum possible adding time 5 and spirit 4 depending on how you want to describe it as working. Essentially allowing the chemical substance to transform the human into a vampire and acting as the embrace. Paradox can take care of the 16th gen as a mild side effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T01:41:50-07:00","id":1451290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451278#post1451278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From Vampire: Just hand wave it as that's how it worked, nothing in vampire really covers this except for specifically disallowing it in some editions (has to be drank from the vein of the vampire).</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but I believe that some Thaumaturgical/Vicissitude/Alchemical formulas could be also used to &quot;simulate&quot; the veins. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451278#post1451278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a Mage: Prime 5, Matter 4 and Life 4 effect minimum possible adding time 5 and spirit 4 depending on how you want to describe it as working. Essentially allowing the chemical substance to transform the human into a vampire and acting as the embrace. Paradox can take care of the 16th gen as a mild side effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I didn't know. Is it your own idea or do you find it somewhere?<br /> <br /> As for Thin-Bloods Special powers I would simply ignore that part. Also, Thin Bloods from earlier editions could also develope their own special powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 06-08-2021, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T19:23:01-07:00","id":1451410,"title":"","content":"Wait I got confused are you using Pre-V5 vampire or V5? Pre-V5 the 1st ed DA 5 dot Quietus power could technically work. Also Vicissitude could theoretically make a &quot;Juice Box&quot; out of vampiric flesh and blood. In V5 thin bloods are different mechanically from actual vampires -- no blood potency and such.<br /> <br /> The Mage advice is according to the minimum by what those levels do, I don't think there is a published ritual for becoming vampires. Life and Matter to make a permanent transformation and Prime to infuse magic into the pattern. Paradox can slightly alter reality as an effect of burning off, including slightly altering a spell in an unintended way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","user":"Gubenyochi","date":".  Fixed spelling errors 06-08-2021, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T00:02:09-07:00","id":1451419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451410#post1451410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait I got confused are you using Pre-V5 vampire or V5? Pre-V5 the 1st ed DA 5 dot Quietus power could technically work. Also Vicissitude could theoretically make a &quot;Juice Box&quot; out of vampiric flesh and blood. In V5 thin bloods are different mechanically from actual vampires -- no blood potency and such.<br /> <br /> The Mage advice is according to the minimum by what those levels do, I don't think there is a published ritual for becoming vampires. Life and Matter to make a permanent transformation and Prime to infuse magic into the pattern. Paradox can slightly alter reality as an effect of burning off, including slightly altering a spell in an unintended way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP states they're mainly using V20 because it meshes with the other *20 books.<br /> <br /> In V20, there are rules for the 16th Generation in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. They have both a smaller blood pool they can use for Disciplines and blood buffing (4 points, as opposed to the 6 of 15th Gens) and can only learn Disciplines up to the second dot. They can still use their remaining blood points for rising each night, but they have the Thin Blood Flaw as standard (double all blood costs).<br /> <br /> In V5, the distinction is meaningless, as all Thin Bloods use the same mechanics with a pick and mix approach to strengths and weaknesses to represent their innate variation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T19:39:22-07:00","id":1451796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451260#post1451260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But good luck. Keep us posted on how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>For now I'm running preludes, it will take a while to actually use one of this ideas. I just wanted to be prepared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T14:24:39-07:00","id":1453483,"title":"","content":"I sometimes wish 16th Gen had been given a closer look at since in many ways they seem like a watered-down 15th generation with mostly the same drawbacks and fewer benefits. At the very least I'd have expected 16th gen to have more 'human' traits as well as greater resistance to sunlight (say bashing instead of lethal, which is also what 15th gen suffered sunlight as instead of aggravated.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T16:38:44-07:00","id":1453491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1451235#post1451235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want a ready-made solution, use this one: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/513f57ebe4b0970eaf232dec/t/5c05ae8f898583fc3fb57776/1543876240815/V5%2Bto%2BV20%2BConversion%2BDoc.pdf&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://static1.squarespace.com/stat...sion%2BDoc.pdf</a><br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>These rules are cool! Who are the authors?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T04:26:21-07:00","id":1453535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1453483#post1453483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sometimes wish 16th Gen had been given a closer look at since in many ways they seem like a watered-down 15th generation with mostly the same drawbacks and fewer benefits. At the very least I'd have expected 16th gen to have more 'human' traits as well as greater resistance to sunlight (say bashing instead of lethal, which is also what 15th gen suffered sunlight as instead of aggravated.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd been toying with giving them (Humanity) minutes in the sun before they start burning. The problem with making sunlight bashing damage is that it's halved after soak, so at that point, you may as well remove it as a weakness.<br /> <br /> I'm also not overly keen on the doubled blood cost expenditures. Even ghouls and revenants don't need to do that. The reduced blood available for Disciplines and blood buffs is enough, I think.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'd let 16th Gens heal bashing as mortals, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1453491#post1453491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These rules are cool! Who are the authors?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone on Reddit. I can't remember who, exactly. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T21:47:31-07:00","id":1454794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1453535#post1453535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd been toying with giving them (Humanity) minutes in the sun before they start burning. The problem with making sunlight bashing damage is that it's halved after soak, so at that point, you may as well remove it as a weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't assume all bashing damage is the same though. The 'halved soak' is a very context specific (blunt trauma more or less, and reflects the fact vampires don't have vital organs or bleed out/shock the way humans do if hit by blunt trauma. It's also why Vampires treat gunfire as blunt (except the head) even though its lethal for humans. Sunlight isn't blunt trauma. It isn't really even heat damage. It's metaphysical 'god's curse' damage and thus wouldn't be subject to the half-soak IMHO. <br /> <br /> That said I suppose you could also give them a lower difficulty to soak lethal although I'm not sure that's really worth the mechanical drawbacks the 16th gen suffer compared to 15th. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also not overly keen on the doubled blood cost expenditures. Even ghouls and revenants don't need to do that. The reduced blood available for Disciplines and blood buffs is enough, I think.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'd let 16th Gens heal bashing as mortals, too. </div> </div> </div>I think it was a mistake to make 15th and 16th gen mandatory thinbloods (and thus automatically suffering the double BP drawback) rather than giving them options. I've always treated being thin-blooded as independent of generation with different combinations of benefits or drawbacks to use (Time of Thin Blood for examples mentions not all Thinbloods benefit from immortality, or have fangs... some of those might be substituted for the double-BP cost too.) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T00:09:50-07:00","id":1454803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451194-first-16th-generation-cainite?p=1454794#post1454794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't assume all bashing damage is the same though. The 'halved soak' is a very context specific (blunt trauma more or less, and reflects the fact vampires don't have vital organs or bleed out/shock the way humans do if hit by blunt trauma. It's also why Vampires treat gunfire as blunt (except the head) even though its lethal for humans. Sunlight isn't blunt trauma. It isn't really even heat damage. It's metaphysical 'god's curse' damage and thus wouldn't be subject to the half-soak IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're describing sounds like lethal damage to me, but I guess it's your table. In Revised and V20, all bashing is halved, even if from firearms. There's no special, unhalved bashing because bashing is treated as normal damage, the same as lethal, for healing. If you remove what makes it unique (the halving), it's just lethal.<br /> <br /> In V20, the damage rules on 284-5 don't even seem to say that extra bashing damage wraps around the track to convert existing bashing levels to lethal (or lethal to aggravated, etc), though that was there in Revised, I think. That's the only benefit of it being unhalved bashing instead of lethal that I can see in pre-V5 RAW.<br /> <br /> However, V20DA says that if you'd be Incapacitated with bashing damage, it only counts as Crippled instead. I guess if you also allow Thin Bloods to heal bashing as mortals, those two together (perhaps plus the Revised rule of wrapping around damage) would give it more weight? Otherwise, as I say, unhalved bashing damage is no different to lethal, mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-13-2021, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}